<p>LOOKING AHEAD →</p>
<p>Aristotle has told us that eudaimonia is activity of the soul in accordance with reason, performed well. The next page asks the obvious follow-up: what does it mean for reason to be performed <em>well</em>? Aristotle's answer is virtue, and the way we get virtue is not what you might expect.</p>
